This original incident summary is retained for history. Its "one issue" conclusion
is superseded by the [signed review](/kb/incidents/4471-review), which separates
the parser and booking-form hint causes. Use that review and the updated triage
runbook for current guidance. The original account follows.

Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. By
4 October the desk had **412 reports**.

**Merged as one issue.** The parser reads dates month first, and our tenants write the day
first. The fix is queued.

<Callout>
Known. One issue, one fix queued.
</Callout>

